  "notes": "The exact Kusakabe photograph on Qualla and the Rijksmuseum’s separate 1891–1900 albumen print show the Main’s twin faceted bays, temple-like tile roof, deep cornice and veranda. The standing hotel’s architecture guide and renovation account describe the other mapped wings and their period-specific roofs."
